meta {
  name: Get Admission Status (All Cycles, Student)
  type: http
  seq: 25
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/student/application-forms/status?college_id={{collegeId}}
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  ~college_id: {{collegeId}}
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{studentAccessToken}}
}

docs {
  Same as Get Admission Status, but with no admissionCycleId in the path —
  use this whenever you don't have a specific cycle id in hand yet.

  `college_id` (optional query param):
  - omitted -> spans every admission cycle across every college the
    student has ever applied to (general "my applications" status screen)
  - provided -> narrows to that one college, across all of ITS cycles
    (covers a college running several concurrent admission cycles) —
    this is the one to use for an "Apply" button/page scoped to a
    specific college where you know the college_id but not which cycle
    the student may have already started under

  Use the cycle-scoped version
  (/application-forms/{{admissionCycleId}}/application/status) instead
  when you already know the specific cycle — note that one now returns a
  richer shape (application/assessment/interview/amountDetails); this
  all-cycles endpoint deliberately keeps the original flat shape:

  `data` is `null` if the student hasn't started any application in scope
  yet. Otherwise an array, each entry shaped:

  {
    applicationId, applicationNumber,
    collegeId, collegeName,
    admissionCycleId, admissionCycleName,
    courses: [{ courseId, courseName, courseCode, isPrimary, status }, ...],
    formStatus, feePaymentStatus,
    pendingAction: "payment" | "personal_details" | "family_details"
                 | "address_details" | "qualification_details"
                 | "entrance_exam_details" | "declaration" | "submit" | "none",
    formSteps: [{ key, label, status: "completed"|"current"|"pending" }, ...],
    createdAt
  }

  `pendingAction` is the single next mandatory thing to do (cheap,
  currentStep-derived). `formSteps` is the FULL per-screen breakdown of
  every screen in the 10-screen form (+ payment/documents), in display
  order:

    payment, personal_details, family_details, address_details,
    tenth_grade, twelfth_grade, undergraduate, pg, diploma,
    achievements_details, entrance_exam_details, documents, declaration

  Status per entry:
  - "completed": done
  - "current": the one the student should be on right now (only ever set
    for the sequential mandatory screens: payment, personal, family,
    address, entrance_exam, declaration)
  - "pending": not done yet, not currently blocking

  The 5 academic-record screens (tenth_grade/twelfth_grade/undergraduate/
  pg/diploma) are never "current" — a student only needs to fill in
  whichever ONE applies to them, so these are just completed/pending based
  on whether that section has actually been saved. achievements_details is
  optional and supplementary — also never "current", never blocks
  progression. documents is a checklist (required-vs-uploaded), computed
  independently of currentStep, also never "current".

  Each entry carries its own collegeId/collegeName and
  admissionCycleId/admissionCycleName (every college runs fully independent
  admission cycles), so entries from different colleges/cycles can be told
  apart and grouped by the client.
}
